@* The window's HintView: a "?" beside a label, and the advice behind it, which stays open until it is closed again - a
   tooltip vanished the moment the pointer moved toward several sentences somebody reads while deciding. A disclosure
   rather than a script: the browser opens and closes it, and the text is in the page for whoever reads it aloud.

   Pointed at, the "?" also shows the advice as the browser's tooltip: what a field asks for is read over its name, and a
   line under every field pushed the form down a screen for words most people read once. *@

<details class="@($"hint-mark {Class}".TrimEnd())">
    <summary aria-label="@($"About {Of}")" title="@Text">?</summary>
    <p class="hint-mark-text">@Text</p>
</details>

@code {
    /// <summary>The advice, as Core keeps it (SettingsAdvice, PhaseAdvice, RoleAdvice) or a view model says it.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Text { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>What the advice is about - the label beside it - for the "?" to be named by.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Of { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>A class of the advice's own (settings-credentials: where a credential must not go).</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }
}
